### Shopper self-registration — public, stateless, store-scoped. Addressed on the store host, through spg, the
### way the storefront's own register page calls it. No cookie, no token.

### Register a shopper for STORE_ID → 201, empty body
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?store={{STORE_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}",
  "email": "jane-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}@example.com",
  "password": "secret-1",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### The seeded shopper's username again → 409 CUA.REGISTRATION.USERNAME_TAKEN
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?store={{STORE_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "email": "someone-else@example.com",
  "password": "secret-1"
}

### The seeded shopper's email again → 409 CUA.REGISTRATION.EMAIL_TAKEN
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?store={{STORE_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "someone-else",
  "email": "user@mail.com",
  "password": "secret-1"
}

### Isolation: the same username is free on the second store → 201 (uniqueness is per store, never per pod)
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?store={{STORE_ID_2}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}",
  "email": "jane-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}@example.com",
  "password": "secret-1"
}

### A malformed body → 400 COMMON.VALIDATION_FAILED with fieldErrors for email and password
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?store={{STORE_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jo",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### No store → 400 (the store resolver refuses; nothing can register "nowhere")
POST {{LANDING_UI_URL}}/cua/api/v1/public/registration?lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nobody",
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "secret-1"
}
